 Add `--json` to get a JSON object instead.
 
+### Caching
+
+Parsing dominates the runtime on large files. Pass `--cache` to store the
+parsed records on disk and reuse them on the next run over the same file. The
+cache directory is configurable via the `LOGSLICE_CACHE_DIR` environment
+variable or `XDG_CACHE_HOME`.
+
+```
+logslice --cache huge.log --count-by level   # parses and caches
+logslice --cache huge.log --level error      # served from the cache
+```
+
+Use `--cache-ttl SECONDS` to set cache expiration (default 3600 seconds).
+
+Cached results are stored as JSON in the cache directory (default `~/.cache/logslice`), one entry per log file. The cache key includes the file's size and modification time, so editing or appending to a log invalidates its entry. Entries expire after the configured TTL; delete the directory to clear the cache.
+
 ## Development
 
